CHAPTER I GENERAL PROVISIONS

Article 1 (Purpose) The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters mandated by the Act on Promotion and Support of Water Reuse and those necessary for the enforcement thereof.

CHAPTER II WATER REUSE PLAN

Article 2 (Matters to be included in water reuse master plan) (1) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 5(5)6 of the Act on Promotion and Support of Water Reuse (hereinafter referred to as the "Act"), means the following:
  1. Researching and developing to promote the production and use of treated water under subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "treated water") and matters for utilization thereof;
  2. Measures to cultivate technical personnel relating to water reuse;
  3. Plans to strengthen international competitiveness of the water reuse industry and to support the industry to enter overseas markets;
  4. Strategies to publicize water reuse.

Article 3 (Formulation of water reuse management plans) (1) When the Special Metropolitan City Mayor, Metropolitan City Mayors, the Special Self-Governing City Mayor, the Jeju Special Self-Governing Province Governor, or the heads of Sis/Guns (excluding the heads of Guns in Metropolitan Cities; hereinafter the same shall apply) formulate a water reuse management plan under Article 6(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "water reuse management plan"), such plan shall include the following: <Amended on Jul. 16, 2024>
  1. Current status of water supply and demand, and outlook for water use in the relevant jurisdictional area;
  2. Current status of installing and operating water reuse facilities;
  3. Outlook for demand for water reuse;
  4. Practical target quantity of water reuse by field and supply plans by use;
  5. Impact of water reuse on maintaining river flows in the lower reaches of rivers and on the use of river water;
  6. Matters concerning measures for promoting water reuse for each stage and concerning business plans;
  7. Matters concerning calculating expenses to be incurred in water reuse business and concerning fundraising plans;
  8. Matters concerning publicity for water reuse;
  9. Other matters prescribed by municipal ordinance with regard to water reuse.
  (2) Where the Special Metropolitan City Mayor, Metropolitan City Mayors, the Special Self-Governing City Mayor, the Jeju Special Self-Governing Province Governor, or the heads of Sis/Guns intend to formulate or amend a water reuse management plan pursuant to Article 6(1) of the Act, they shall first hear the opinions of the relevant Special Metropolitan City Mayor, Metropolitan City Mayors, Special Self-Governing City Mayor, Do Governors, or Special Self-Governing Province Governors, or the heads of the relevant Sis/Guns. <Amended on Jul. 16, 2024>
  (3) When the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment intends to grant approval or approval for modification of a water reuse management plan under Article 6(1) of the Act, the Minister may seek the opinion of the Korea Environment Corporation established under the Korea Environment Corporation Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Korea Environment Corporation") to examine the technical matters. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>

Article 4 (Persons entitled to formulate water reuse management plans) (1) "Important matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" under the latter part of Article 6(1) of the Act, means the following:
  1. Changing a period to achieve the practical target quantity of water reuse by field (only applicable to changing the period exceeding two years);
  2. Changing supply plans by use;
  3. Changing expenses exceeding 30/100 of the expenses to be incurred in a water reuse business.
  (2) Where a sewerage system extends over at least 2 jurisdictions, a person who is to formulate a water reuse management plan shall determine the plan following consultation with the relevant Special Metropolitan City Mayor, Metropolitan City Mayors, Special Self-Governing City Mayor, Do Governors, or Special Self-Governing Province Governors, or the heads of the relevant Sis/Guns (hereinafter referred to as the "heads of relevant local governments); provided, where no consultation is held between the heads of relevant local governments, such plan shall be determined following consultation with: <Amended on Jul. 16, 2024; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Where the heads of the relevant local governments are the heads of Sis/Guns under the jurisdiction of the same Do or Special Self-Governing Province: The head of a Si/Gun, designated by the competent Do Governor or Special Self-Governing Province Governor;
  2. Where the heads of the relevant local governments are the heads of Sis/Guns under the jurisdictions of other Dos or Special Self-Governing Provinces: A Do Governor, a Special Self-Governing Province Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun determined by consultation between the competent Do Governors or between the competent Do Governors and the competent Special Self-Governing Province Governors;
  3. Where the heads of the relevant local governments are the Special Metropolitan City Mayor, Metropolitan City Mayors, the Special Self-Governing City Mayor, or the heads of Sis/Guns: The Special Metropolitan City Mayor, Metropolitan City Mayors, the Special Self-Governing City Mayor, Do Governors, Special Self-Governing Province Governors, or the heads of Sis/Guns, determined by consultation between the competent Special Metropolitan City Mayor, Metropolitan City Mayors, Special Self-Governing City Mayor, and Do Governors or Special Self-Governing Province Governors having jurisdictions over such Sis/Guns;
  4. Where no consultation is held under subparagraphs 2 and 3: The Special Metropolitan City Mayor, Metropolitan City Mayors, the Special Self-Governing City Mayor, Governors, Special Self-Governing Province Governors, or the heads of Sis/Guns, designated by the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment.

